The general rule for multiplying a \(2 \times 2\) matrix by a \(2 \times 1\) vector is:

\[
\begin{pmatrix}
a & b \\
c & d
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
x \\
y
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
ax + by \\
cx + dy
\end{pmatrix}
\]

